{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3503","id":4655676623,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz888AAAABFX_8zw","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3503","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3503.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3503.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3503","number":3503,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"state: send a node its own self after its routes change","user":{"login":"Sarcouy","id":25173195,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MTczMTk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25173195?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy","html_url":"https://github.com/Sarcouy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sarcouy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\n- [x] added unit tests\n- [x] added integration tests\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md\n\nFixes #3502\n\n### What\n\nA node never received its own updated self node after its routes were approved, so on its live map session `Self.AllowedIPs` stayed without the approved exit routes and `tailscale status` never printed \"offers exit node\" until tailscaled restarted. Since 0.29.4 the same happens when the node withdraws and re-advertises the routes, which used to be the workaround.\n\n### Why\n\nThe mapper only adds the self node when `Change.OriginNode` is the receiving node (`batcher.go` `isSelfUpdate`, `policyChangeResponse(..., includeSelf)`). Two paths lose that origin:\n\n- `State.SetApprovedRoutes` ends with `if routeChange || !c.IsFull() { c = change.PolicyChange() }`, which is always taken, so the gRPC/CLI approval fans out a bare `PolicyChange()`.\n- `State.UpdateNodeFromMapRequest` returns the policy change from `updatePolicyManagerNodes` before `buildMapRequestChangeResponse` could produce `change.NodeAdded(id)`. Since 4411264e / 905ab92f (#3450, backported in #3467) `HasPolicyChange` compares `ExitRoutes()`, so a re-advertise now takes that early return.\n\nThe fix stamps `OriginNode` on the change in both places, the same way `SetNodeTags` does since #2996. Nothing else changes: the batcher already turns an origin into `policyChangeResponse(includeSelf=true)`, peers keep receiving the same policy response, `Change.Merge` already preserves `OriginNode`.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `hscontrol/state`: `TestMapRequestRouteChangeIsSelfUpdate` asserts `OriginNode` on the change returned by `SetApprovedRoutes` and by three map requests (announce, withdraw, re-announce). Fails on `main` (`OriginNode: 0`), passes with the fix.\n- `hscontrol/servertest`: `TestRoutes/advertiser_learns_own_approved_exit_routes` drives two real control clients: the advertiser sees `0.0.0.0/0` and `::/0` in its own `SelfNode.AllowedIPs` after the approval, loses them after a withdrawal and gets them back after a re-advertise, all on the same session; the observer still sees them on the peer.\n- `integration`: `TestSubnetRouterMultiNetworkExitNode` now also asserts `Self.ExitNodeOption` and `Self.AllowedIPs` on the exit node itself after `ApproveRoutes`, before the peer is told to use it.\n\n### Notes\n\n- The open draft #3501 rewrites the same lines; both hunks rebase onto it as one assignment after its `if/else` in `SetApprovedRoutes` and one before its kept `return policyChange`. Happy to rebase whichever lands second.\n- The `SetApprovedRoutes` part affects 0.29.x too: a backport to `release-branch/0.29` would be welcome.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-09-27T17:53:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T17:53:22Z","closed_at":"2026-09-27T17:53:22Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1876bc4633aa25817ffcd69ba0132285cd357a51","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions